The strategy is the optimal one for **misère Nim** with 4 piles:

- If **all non-empty piles are size 1**, then:
  - an **even** number of 1-heaps is winning, so remove one whole heap;
  - an **odd** number is losing, so any legal move is as good as possible.
- If there is **exactly one pile bigger than 1**:
  - if the number of 1-heaps is **even**, reduce the big pile to **1**;
  - if the number of 1-heaps is **odd**, reduce the big pile to **0**.
- Otherwise, when there are **at least two piles bigger than 1**, play like normal Nim:
  - compute the xor (nim-sum);
  - if it is nonzero, move to a position with xor 0;
  - if it is already 0, the position is losing, so return any legal move.

This is the standard perfect-play solution for misère Nim and always returns a legal move whenever one exists.
